  "historical_output_text": " Once at school camp on Vancouver’s Stanley Island as I approached 9-years-age the night fell heavily upon us as my parents were preparing our small, two-person shelter under some large pine needles and I found it rather boring; so instead with some misstep of the toe that sent it off in the air into that space, that darkness under those bunched up leaves a little piece was gone and left the hole where only light was once. As time wore down my mind had filled that night in my dreams up as much and the memory is that my little finger is in some strange shape. That memory was one night only though it had lasted much, and that mistake made was my lesson; for every day has some light to find but first must see its loss.\nWhat did this author gain in the process?\nAs I reflected over time about what the incident of that one missing tree",
